{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/408071-adhering-to-human-interpretations-of-kiths-seemings","id":408071,"title":"Adhering to human interpretations of Kiths / Seemings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-16T12:44:12-08:00","id":408071,"title":"Adhering to human interpretations of Kiths / Seemings?","content":"This is a question that came from the Changeling Slang Thread<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/148067-changeling-slang\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...angeling-slang</a> . I didn't post it there to avoid derailing the primary purpose of the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fairy</b> - A term used to refer to a Changeling who insists on adhering human interpretations of their Kiths / Seemings. </div> </div> </div>This one I didn't really get. A Changeling is supposed to be a changed being as a result of her durance. How could she have human interpretations of anything? Can you give me an example. This is possibly a Changeling with high Clarity and low Wryd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4811,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4811-thinking_point","user":"Thinking_Point","date":". 02-16-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4811-thinking_point","name":"Thinking_Point","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T13:12:05-08:00","id":408110,"title":"","content":"I'm sure Nyrufa will be around to clarify what (he? she?) had in mind, but it scans to me like a changeling who interprets her new state through the emphasis of her kith's capabilities and the impressions of others. A changeling who thinks &quot;I'm brineborn now and that's not going to change, I guess I better find an apartment down by the docks,&quot; regardless of what she actually personally feels about living around the water.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I could see it used to denote a changeling who feels there's a sharper divide between the psychology and culture of changelings and the non-fae, and allows herself to delve deep into the mindset of the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are other changelings who see that divide as much blurrier. A changeling dances on the edge of a knife, neither human nor inhuman, and yet both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:41:24-08:00","id":410545,"title":"","content":"I read that as meaning that, rather than categorising one's self as a changeling shaped by a unique durance (&quot;I am Sally of the Deep, who survived the realm of the Water-Wide Lord&quot;), this changeling sticks to general mythological concepts made by non-changelings when thinking of themselves. (&quot;I am a mermaid. I should probably be wearing a clam-shell bikini and try to lure sailors.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/